course: dictionary
lesson: 7766
title: Pursue: chase or keep going
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pursue is a verb, which means a doing word. Its first meaning is to chase someone or something to catch them. «The police pursued the thief through the town.» The police are running after the thief to catch them.
explain: Pursue can also mean to keep working at something over a long time. «She wants to pursue a career in science.» Nobody is being chased here. She is aiming for a job and will work towards it for years. Pursuing a dream means the same thing.
explain: The words around pursue give you clues. A thief, a rabbit or a chase points to running after something. A dream, a career or a hobby points to working at something over time. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In a company announcement, «Pursuing other opportunities» usually means the worker has been fired or pushed out, even though it sounds like a happy plan. When the context seems strange, think about what is really going on and check your dictionary if you are unsure.
fact: Pursue means to chase or follow someone or something to catch them.
fact: To pursue a goal, hobby or job means to try to achieve it over a long time.
fact: Pursue is a verb: pursue, pursues, pursued, pursuing.
fact: «In hot pursuit» means chasing closely after someone.
fact: In formal writing, to pursue a matter means to keep asking about it or dealing with it.
exercise: «The fox began to pursue the rabbit across the field.» What does pursue mean here? | *To chase, to run after it to catch it | To ask the rabbit questions | To stop and rest | To fall asleep under a bush
exercise: «Ravi wants to pursue a career in science.» What does pursue suggest? | To finish all his science today | To forget about science | To chase a science teacher around the school | *To work towards a job over a long time
exercise: Which phrase means chasing closely after someone? | *in hot pursuit | with a hot drink | at a slow pace
test: «The detective will pursue the case until the thief is found.» What does pursue mean here? | To play a game with it | *To keep working on it until it is solved | To forget about it completely | To say sorry for it
test: Aisha has a dream to be an artist. She wants to ___ her dream. Which word fits best? | *pursue | lose | hide
exam: In a company announcement, «Pursuing other opportunities» usually suggests what? | The company is going on holiday | The worker has been given a pay rise | The worker has won a prize | *The worker has been fired or pushed to leave
